# Approved story → git workflow

When you **finish implementing an approved story** from [`docs/prd.md`](docs/prd.md) (Epics 1–10), **do not stop at uncommitted local changes**. Complete the full git workflow in the same session unless the user explicitly says not to commit yet.

“Approved” means the story is approved in the PRD (PM sign-off / D-40 epics) or the user treats the story as approved (e.g. “work on story 9.4”, “merge it like 9.2”).

## Required steps (same as CLAUDE.md)

1. `git checkout main && git pull`
2. Branch: `story/<epic>.<story>-<short-slug>` (e.g. `story/10.1-documentation`)
3. Commit with a clear message: `Story X.Y: <short description>`
4. `git push -u origin <branch>`
5. `gh pr create --base main` with Summary + Test plan
6. `gh pr merge --merge`
7. `git checkout main && git pull`

Never commit directly to `main`. Never commit `.env` or secrets.

## When to skip

- User says **do not commit**, **draft only**, or **wait for PM approval**
- Story work is **incomplete** or **blocked** (document what’s left instead of merging)
- Only **questions or reviews** with no story implementation

## After merge

Tell the user the PR URL, merge commit on `main`, and what was included.
